    {
      "page_title": "Tombstones: Deleting a Key",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sizing The Window"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Consumer downtime",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Under the window",
              "Sees the delete"
            ],
            [
              "Over the window",
              "Phantom key kept"
            ],
            [
              "Streams rebuild",
              "Must fit inside it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set it above your worst expected consumer outage",
            "And above the time to rebuild a Streams state store",
            "A missed tombstone leaves stale state nobody notices"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consumer Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Handle nulls: `value.field()` on a tombstone is an NPE",
            "That NPE is the #1 compacted-topic crash",
            "In Streams a null into a KTable deletes the key"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-console-consumer.sh --topic users \\",
            "  --property print.key=true \\",
            "  --property print.value=true  # null shown"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Erasure On A Deadline",
          "items": [
            "Tombstone the key first",
            "Then set `max.compaction.lag.ms` inside the legal window",
            "Forces a pass even when the dirty ratio is low"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Settings",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Policy",
            "Retains",
            "Workload"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`delete`",
              "All versions in window",
              "Events, metrics"
            ],
            [
              "`compact`",
              "Latest per key, forever",
              "State, offsets"
            ],
            [
              "`compact,delete`",
              "Latest, time-bounded",
              "Changelogs"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`delete` answers 'what happened recently'",
            "`compact` answers 'what is true now'",
            "Per-partition ordering is identical for both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Disk Shape And Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "`delete`",
              "items": [
                "Bounded by window",
                "Near-free unlink",
                "Partial replay"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "`compact`",
              "items": [
                "Bounded by cardinality",
                "Constant recopy I/O",
                "Full state replay"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compacted size ≈ unique keys × average value size",
            "Compaction burns background CPU and disk forever",
            "Deleting a segment is one cheap unlink"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Key Cardinality Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bounded keys — user ID, device ID, account — compact well",
            "A UUID per event is unbounded and grows forever",
            "Unbounded keys on `compact` is the classic misuse",
            "Need history plus a bound? Use `compact,delete`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Delete vs Compact vs Both",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick By Bootstrap",
          "text": "If a consumer must build complete state from the topic, use `compact`. Otherwise use `delete`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Duplicates You Get"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Read from",
            "`delete`",
            "`compact`"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Offset 0",
              "Many per key",
              "≤ 1 in the tail"
            ],
            [
              "Head",
              "Many per key",
              "Many per key"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Policy is per-topic, never per-record",
            "A mixed workload needs two topics, not one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Migrating An Old Topic"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Switching `delete` to `compact` reuses the existing log",
            "Pre-existing null-keyed records make the cleaner fail",
            "Purge or re-key that partition first, then flip the policy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-configs.sh --alter \\",
            "  --entity-type topics --entity-name s \\",
            "  --add-config \\",
            "  'cleanup.policy=compact,delete'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Changing It Safely",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Live change, no restart, via `kafka-configs.sh --alter`",
            "Revert with `--delete-config retention.ms`",
            "Re-typing the old value freezes today's default forever"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-configs.sh --alter \\",
            "  --entity-type topics --entity-name t \\",
            "  --delete-config retention.ms  # inherit"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Purging A Topic"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "How",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Fast",
              "`retention.ms=1000`",
              "Then delete config"
            ],
            [
              "Surgical",
              "`kafka-delete-records.sh`",
              "Truncate below offset"
            ],
            [
              "Nuclear",
              "Delete the topic",
              "Loses configs, ACLs"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-delete-records.sh \\",
            "  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\",
            "  --offset-json-file offsets.json"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Disk Full Is An Outage",
          "text": "The log dir is marked offline, replicas drop, and `min.insync.replicas` can block every producer on the topic."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Alert Before It Hurts"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Log-dir free percent, well ahead of the cliff",
            "`UnderReplicatedPartitions` above zero",
            "Retention changes reclaim in minutes, not seconds",
            "A stalled `__consumer_offsets` cleaner slows every commit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Metrics That Tell Truth"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Metric",
            "Reads as"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Log,name=Size`",
              "Bytes on disk"
            ],
            [
              "`NumLogSegments`",
              "Files per partition"
            ],
            [
              "`LogStartOffset`",
              "Advances = deleted"
            ],
            [
              "`LogEndOffset`",
              "Head of the log"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Operating Retention: Ops and Failure Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`log.retention.check.interval.ms` too high delays reclaim",
            "Too low burns I/O scanning every partition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Retention Meets The Rest"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reassignment copies the FULL retained log — slow, bandwidth-heavy",
            "Tiered storage KIP-405: `local.retention.ms` vs `retention.ms`",
            "`transactional.id.expiration.ms` and `.snapshot` clean separately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "OffsetOutOfRangeException",
          "items": [
            "Retention outran a lagging consumer",
            "Fix the lag or widen the window first",
            "Then set `auto.offset.reset` deliberately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sizing Traps",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`retention.bytes` is per-partition — multiply by partitions and RF",
            "A huge `segment.bytes` outlives `retention.ms` by weeks",
            "The active segment is immortal; partitions never hit zero",
            "Unbounded key cardinality on `compact` is unbounded disk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Clock And Cleaner Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One future-dated `CreateTime` freezes a whole segment",
            "A stalled cleaner is silent — only the dirty-ratio metric shows it",
            "Retention runs per replica, so leader and follower sizes differ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not Deduplication",
          "text": "Compaction removes older values of the SAME key. Two records with different keys and identical values both survive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas, Checklist, and Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Assumptions To Unlearn"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Belief",
            "Truth"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "One record per key",
              "The head keeps duplicates"
            ],
            [
              "Null value = corruption",
              "It is a tombstone"
            ],
            [
              "Gone at `retention.ms`",
              "Best effort, later"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ship Checklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set both `retention.ms` and `retention.bytes`",
            "Keep `segment.ms` well below `retention.ms`",
            "`delete.retention.ms` > max consumer downtime",
            "Alert on dirty ratio, disk free, URP, consumer lag"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "retention.ms=604800000      # 7 d SLA",
            "retention.bytes=10737418240 # per part",
            "segment.ms=3600000         # 1 h rolls",
            "delete.retention.ms=604800000"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Model"
        },
        {
